{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > make_review.py <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\nrationale='''Reviewed fixed artifact 2e210f3af48042e4a0603d11a5eed235, its retained harness lines 28-59, 69-106 and 108-143, fixed plan and raw stdout for CheckRun 26ad6abcd0bc44fb845a278c177d2f63. The accepted responsibility is context/recipient preservation on actual quorum prefix release, grounded by prefix-confirmation identity expectations, safe-read context expectations and the exact-context consumer; no eventual deadline is inferred. Launch/bootstrap create three voters. The driver saves real updates into TestLogDB, applies generated bootstrap config entries and empty no-op, then calls Commit and NotifyRaftLastApplied. Tick and authentic vote/replication messages establish term-2 leadership and index-4 commitment. Assertions check reached setup and admission. No test-only election override or state injection is used. Peer.ReadIndex generates the forwarded requests. Both first-context heartbeats are discarded by fixed policy; later messages retain generation order. Transport loss is permitted. Delaying replication until persistence strengthens setup ordering without excluding the overlapping reads. No crash or concurrent worker exists.\n\nThe release observation copies pending statuses before Peer.Handle of an authentic HeartbeatResp, then observes removal while still the same-term leader. Source inspection shows this path removes statuses through quorum prefix release, not reset/cancellation. Original status ctx/from is captured independently of replies. Events 5 and 6 establish release of two statuses with current-term commitment. Identity fields run/operation/request_node correlate results 7 and 8 independently of context, with one operation per distinct destination. The assertion compares complete decimal Low/High context content. Serialization also detects extra multiplicity, but the actual witness has exa